<CaseStudyDesigns
  eyebrow="A) PRODUCT SCANNER"
  title="Bridging Intent to Action through Instant Verdict"
  description={`To serve a user who values proactive health over panic, I had to design the core scanning and search flows, to turn complex nutrition data into instant, confident decisions. By streamlining the entire experience, we ensured that every scan and search seamlessly connects the user's health goals with better everyday choices.`}

  steps={[
    {
      label: "A) Accommodating Varied Scanning Scenarios",
      labelColor: "#fcd34d",
      title1: "Challenges",
      description1: `• Low lighting or blurry camera in real-world settings.
      • Torn, wrinkled, or poorly printed barcodes that fail to read.`,
      title2: "Solution",
      description2: "A unified scanner that automatically detects the product or barcode, paired with intuitive, thumb-zone toggle for manual overrides and a text-search option.",
      title3: "Why this works?",
      description3: "It respcts high-velocity user behaviour.",
      image: "/Designs/design1.png",
    },

    {
      label: "B) Navigating Product Match Discrepancies",
      labelColor: "#fcd34d",
      title1: "Challenges",
      description1: `• Discrepancies when a scan matches multiple similar variants.
      • Guessing incorrectly undermines accuracy & trust.`,
      title2: "Iteration-1",
      description2: "An error screen asking the user to rescan when the system fails to map with a single, definitive match.",
      title3: "Iteration-2",
      description3: "Horizontal carousel of top 5 matches, requiring the user to compare & select the correct one before proceeding.",

      image: "/Designs/design2.png",
    },

    {
      label: "B) Navigating Product Match Discrepancies",
      labelColor: "#fcd34d",
      title1: "Iteration-3 (Final Solution)",
      description1: `• A Smart Confirmation screen that displays the highest-confidence match which auto-redirects to the verdict page.
      • If the user identifies a mismatch during this window, a single tap immediately reveals a list of alternative options.`,
      title3: "Why this works?",
      description3: `• Prioritizes speed, resolving 90% of cases without user intervention.
      • Effectively balances system speed with user agency, ensuring that the flow is never interrupted.`,

      image: "/Designs/design3.png",
    },

    {
      label: "C) Resolving 'Product Not Found' into Community Value",
      labelColor: "#fcd34d",
      title1: "Challenges",
      description1: `• Momentum blocked, triggers immediate disappointment.
      • Lose confidence in the app's reliability.`,
      title2: "Solution",
      description2: "An overlay acknowledging that the user has found something unique with a streamlined camera interface, that requests quick snapshots to fix the database gap.",
      title3: "Why this works?",
      description3: "Transforms a moment of UX friction into a psychological positive.",

      image: "/Designs/design4.png",
    },
  ]}
  client:load
/>

<CaseStudySolutions
  eyebrow="FINAL CONCLUSION"
  title="Measuring Impact & Looking Ahead"
  description={`Building the Yelona Inventory & Order Management System (IOMS) proved that great enterprise design isn't about chasing minimalist layout trends or maximizing empty whitespace—it's about operational survival. By replacing fragile, unvalidated spreadsheets with a high-density, utility-first ecosystem, the system directly resolved the central challenge: safeguarding business revenue by killing clerical blindspots before they ever hit the storefront.


Strategic Impact:`}
 solutions={solutions}
  client:load
/>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-10 py-20">
  <div class="border-l-3 border-zinc-700 pl-6 md:pl-8">
  <p class="text-2xl tracking-wider font-google font-bold text-zinc-50">
    New challenges and what's next:
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-400 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed ">
  While the initial deployment stabilized Yelona’s core inventory workflows, the next frontier focuses on expanding the platform's architectural depth and compliance capabilities. The immediate priority is designing a native GST Collection module to seamlessly orchestrate India's multi-tiered tax structures (CGST, SGST, IGST) alongside localized HSN code parameters directly within the procurement pipeline to automatically reconcile internal purchase orders with vendor tax filings. 
  </p>
  </div>
</section>

